assistant: Subject: convert search_products prices from cents on 2026-10-01

Since vendor API version 2026-10-01, `/products` sends `price` in cents (e.g. 119900) instead of dollars (1199), even though the published spec didn't change. `search_products` passed the value straight through, so agents were told a laptop cost $119,900. The fix is in `src/tools/search_products.ts`: it reads the `vendor-api-version` response header and divides prices by 100 when the version is 2026-10-01 or later. Older versions are returned unchanged, so the v1 fixtures give exactly the same output as before. Typecheck, lint and the full test suite pass, including the repro test. `get_product` and `get_order` also return prices but were not changed, and they may have the same cents problem on the new version.

